BUG (pre-existing, NOT NEARS-1487): POST /api/v1/vendor/business_plan returns 403
for a UserApp customer Passport token, so the paid-subscription vendor
registration flow cannot complete from the UserApp.

Observed live on emulator-5556, UserApp debug build of
fix/NEARS-1487-subscription-retry @ dac9cdf4, backend = primary tree
Admin/ on :8000 (shared, unmodified by this ticket).

--- app runtime log (logcat, cleared immediately before the Confirm tap) ---
[NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/vendor/business_plan
[NET] endpoint=/api/v1/vendor/business_plan http_status=403
[FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/vendor/business_plan http_status=403 type=ApiFailure msg="api request failed" correlation_id=2deabb99-eda3-4e3b-a1da-7b8a5867d663

--- backend response body (curl, same endpoint) ---
HTTP 403 {"errors":{"message":"Permission denied"}}

--- observed UI effect ---
Get.currentRoute stayed at /subscription-payment?store-id=4116&package-id=1
after tapping Confirm: no navigation, no redirect_link, user is stuck.

--- mechanism (read, then confirmed live) ---
Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Vendor/SubscriptionController.php
  business_plan() -> authorizeStore()
authorizeStore() resolves the bearer token ONLY against
Vendor::where('auth_token', $token) / VendorEmployee::where('auth_token', ...).
A UserApp caller always sends the CUSTOMER Passport token, so $vendorId is null
and the method returns 403 "Permission denied" before the allowPending branch
(which is only reachable when NO token is sent at all) can apply.
In the real journey the registering user has only a customer token, so the
paid-subscription branch is unreachable from the UserApp.

Note: the app DOES emit the paired AppLogger.failure line above, so the
logging contract is satisfied - this is a functional defect, not a silent
failure path.
